    "body": "I'm not trying to open old wounds, but we're currently discussing whether or not we need some sort of cookie banner in our pretix solutions (both self-hosted and cloud-based).\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/pretix/pretix/issues/95 states that we don't need to inform users about cookies in pretix. If we still use only the cookies mentioned in that issue we're home safe according to https://www.iubenda.com/en/help/5525-cookies-gdpr-requirements#exemptions (we have a “[Privacy](https://pretix.eu/about/en/privacy)” link on all shop pages; cf. https://pretix.eu/ulf-test/8/privacy/, say).\r\n\r\nCan anybody (more versed in both pretix and the cookie law than me) confirm that we still use only the cookies mentioned in https://github.com/pretix/pretix/issues/95 and that having the Privacy link on all shop pages makes pretix comply with the current EU cookie law?\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\nMikkel\r\n\r\n",
